FILES YOU NEED TO WORK ON:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

apb_component.sv:
  Component class, wrapper for APB_Driver and APB_Stim
  together with the channel that they use to communicate.
  You need to complete this class.

apb_env.sv:
  Top-level testbench environment class APB_env, creates an instance 
  of APB_Component.  This class is complete and you do not need to 
  alter it for the first part of the exercise.  For the "If You
  Have Time" section, there is an opportunity to modify this
  class to provide functions that make it easier for a testcase
  to control the stimulus generation.  Look for comments containing
  the string IF YOU HAVE TIME.

apb_tb.sv:


FILES YOU DO NOT NEED TO ALTER:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

dut/apb_dummy.sv:
  Dummy APB slave, provides non-trivial data on read cycles
  and reports all active cycles to the console.
  
bases.sv
  Base class definitions for Transaction, Component and Channel.
  Transaction is a base class for all transaction data classes
  such as APB_Trans.  Channel is a general-purpose FIFO channel
  that carries Transaction objects from one component to another.
  Component is the component base class, as discussed in the
  classroom session, providing hierarchy and run management.
  
apb_harness.sv:
  Test harness and test-signals interface, unchanged from the previous exercise

apb_classes.sv:
  Definitions of classes APB_Trans, APB_Driver, APB_Stim.
  These classes are all complete, but you are encouraged to
  take a close look at APB_Stim to see what has changed to
  take advantage of the Component base class 
  
mem_map_apb_trans.sv:
  This file defines class Mem_map_APB_Trans, derived from
  APB_Trans to provide modified stimulus.  This class definition
  is unchanged from the previous answer, but it has been moved
  into a separate file to reduce clutter in the files you need
  to work on for this lab.
  
